  "live_records": {
    "q-134277": {
      "dom_id": "question-134277",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Peter, Steve, Chelsea, and Laura each bought $3$ ounces of gummies and $4$ ounces of chocolates. In total, they bought\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,$ounces of candy.",
      "worked_solution": "We must write and evaluate an expression representing the total amount of candy.\n\nSince each of them bought $3$ ounces of gummies and $4$ ounces of chocolates, the amount of candy each person bought, in ounces, is:\n\n$$\n{{3}_{⏟}}_{\\text{gummies}}+{{4}_{⏟}}_{\\text{chocolates}}\n$$\n\nSince *each* person purchased this amount of candy, and there are $4$ people, we must multiply the amount of candy by $4.$ Therefore, the total amount of candy is:\n\n$$\n{{(3+4)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{each person}}\\times {{4}_{⏟}}_{\\text{people}}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the expression, we follow the order of operations with parentheses.\n\nFirst, we perform the operations inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+4)\\times 4 & =(3+4)\\times 4 \\\\  & =7\\times 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply:\n\n$$\n7\\times 4=28\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
