    "q-134280": {
      "dom_id": "question-134280",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "John bought $2$ pounds of chocolate almonds while Rose bought $\\frac{7}{5}$ pound of the same product. How many chocolate almonds did they buy altogether? Express your final answer as a mixed number.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        They bought$\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,$pounds of chocolate almonds.",
      "worked_solution": "To determine the amount of chocolate almonds they bought in total, we have to calculate the following sum:\n\n$$\n2+\\frac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nTo add $2$ and $\\frac{7}{5},$ we need to express the whole number $2$ as an equivalent fraction with a denominator of $5.$\n\nFirst, we write $2$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nThen we put this fraction over a denominator of $5$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 5}{1\\times 5}=\\frac{10}{5}\n$$\n\nSo now, we have to find:\n\n$$\n\\frac{10}{5}+\\frac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nTo add two fractions with like denominators, we add the numerators and keep the denominators the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{10}{5}+\\frac{7}{5}=\\frac{10+7}{5}=\\frac{17}{5}\n$$\n\nExpressing our answer as a mixed number, we have\n\n$$\n17÷5=3\\,\\text{R}\\,2=3\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, John and Rose bought $3\\frac{2}{5}$ pounds of chocolate almonds.",
