    "q-134282": {
      "dom_id": "question-134282",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "After Angela takes her share of John's chocolate almonds, the weight of John's remaining chocolate almonds is$\\,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,$than the weight of Rose's chocolate almonds because $1\\frac{1}{6}$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\frac{7}{5}.$",
      "worked_solution": "John has $1\\frac{1}{6}$ pounds of chocolate almonds remaining, and Rose has $\\frac{7}{5}$ pounds of this product.\n\nWe cannot compare the fractions directly as they don't have a common denominator.\n\nWe can make a common denominator of $6\\times 5=30.$\n\nTo put $1\\frac{1}{6}$ over a denominator of $30,$ we first convert to an improper fraction and then multiply the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n1\\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{7}{6}=\\frac{7\\times 5}{6\\times 5}=\\frac{35}{30}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{7}{5}$ over a denominator of $30,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{5}=\\frac{7\\times 6}{5\\times 6}=\\frac{42}{30}\n$$\n\nWe can now compare the fractions $\\frac{35}{30}$ and $\\frac{42}{30}$ by looking at the numerators only.\n\nSince $35<42,$ the correct statement must be:\n\n$$\n\\frac{35}{30}<\\frac{42}{30}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is\n\n\"After Angela takes her part of John's chocolate almonds, the weight of John's remaining chocolate almonds is $<$ than the weight of Rose's chocolate almonds because $1\\frac{1}{6}<\\frac{7}{5}.$\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
