    "q-134283": {
      "dom_id": "question-134283",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Rose decides to eat $\\frac{2}{5}$ of her chocolate almonds. How many pounds of almonds does she decide to eat?\n\n*Remember that Rose has $\\frac{7}{5}$ of a pound of chocolate almonds.*\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Rose decides to eat\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \npounds of chocolate almonds.",
      "worked_solution": "We know that Rose has $\\frac{7}{5}$ of a pound of chocolate almonds.\n\nTo calculate the fraction of a whole pound that Rose decides to eat, we need to multiply $\\frac{2}{5}$ by $\\frac{7}{5}.$\n\nTo multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{7}{5}=\\frac{2\\times 7}{5\\times 5}=\\frac{14}{25}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Rose decides to eat $\\frac{14}{25}$ pounds of chocolate almonds.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
